<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Framework, nullability and analyser settings live in Directory.Build.props. -->

  <!--
    The fifth runtime project. adr/0039: the artefacts that spell things in words — the Input Log
    codec and, from task 8, the crash artifact that wraps it.

    It references Borough.Core and is referenced by both shells, which may never parse or emit a log
    themselves. It does NOT own the save: 05 §7 makes a save an array dump generated from the field
    declaration, and the declaration is in the core, so the save serialiser stays where the thing it
    is generated from lives. The line that keeps this project a boundary rather than a bag is
    *does a human read the tokens*.

    Borough.Analysers is deliberately absent. This project's whole job is to write strings a human
    reads, which is the thing lint 7 forbids in the core — pointing the core's analysers at it would
    fail the build for doing what it exists to do.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Borough.Core\Borough.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
